      "content": "Primary risk factors include the volatility and flash points of the solvents, leading to vapor cloud formation and ignition; inadequate ventilation accelerates the accumulation of flammable vapors above the liquid surface. Thermal runaway risks are heightened by exothermic reactions within the solvents or due to external heat sources interacting with the dense chemical inventory. Furthermore, high-density racking can impede sprinkler coverage and rapid fire spread, significantly reducing the efficacy of standard fire suppression systems by creating fire pockets.",
