      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In high-density racking, achieving uniform sensor coverage is challenging due to the physical obstruction created by tightly packed containers and equipment. Leaks or small thermal events occurring deep within the rack can generate localized plumes that bypass or mask from detectors, leading to delayed alarm activation. This necessitates the use of advanced, spatially distributed detection technologies, such as volumetric or beam detectors, over reliance on basic point sensors. Site-specific CFD modeling is crucial to determine optimal sensor placements that account for vapor distribution patterns within the racks.",
      "source": "target",
